# ======================================================================
# WHICH LEAGUES, IN ONE PLACE.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# There used to be two crontab lines, each carrying its own copy of these
# lists, and they DISAGREED:
#
#   10 8  * * *  LEAGUES="wnba nfl mlb mls"                        --build
#   0,30 8-23 *  LEAGUES="wnba nfl mlb mls" RUN_LEAGUES="wnba nfl"
#
# The build line named no RUN_LEAGUES, so start-slate.sh defaulted it to
# LEAGUES and the builder was told every league was hosted. The filter that
# keeps unhosted rooms off the player's rail was therefore INERT on the one
# line that actually builds the slate each morning — fifteen mute baseball
# rooms would have gone onto the rail at 08:10 on a game night, exactly the
# failure the filter was written to stop. It only ever worked when the
# morning build had failed and the self-heal ran it from the start line's
# environment instead.
#
# One fact, one file. The cron lines now name a schedule, not a policy.
# The environment still wins, so a hand run can still say
# `RUN_LEAGUES="wnba nfl mlb" host/start-slate.sh` for one evening.
# ======================================================================

# Built: schedule docs, rosters and question banks. Cheap — a few writes.
# Build wide: the data is what the backtest and tomorrow's decision run on.
# 28 Aug: epl added. The resolvers were proven on 27 Aug — 10 games, 80
# resolutions, 59 answered, 0 invalid, 0 threw against soccer/eng.1 — and
# the league then sat shadow-only for a day because build-slate.js did not
# know it existed. It does now: the league table has ONE owner, and it is
# host/leagues.js. cfb is known to the code but deliberately NOT built
# here yet — a college Saturday is 25+ games, which is a pick-file
# decision rather than a build-wide one.
# 29 Aug: cfb added. The shadow run cleared the bar the same day (4 games,
# 76 resolutions, 63 answered, 0 invalid, 0 threw) and Boise State at
# Oregon is booked for Sat 5 Sept. A college Saturday is 60+ games, so
# THIS LINE ALONE IS NOT ENOUGH: the pick file is what makes the day the
# day, exactly as the comment on RUN_LEAGUES below warns.
LEAGUES="wnba nfl mlb mls epl cfb"

# Hosted: a node process, a lease, and a feed poll every 30s for four hours.
# ALSO decides what the player's rail offers, because a room nobody hosts
# must never appear as a room. Turn a league on here, not in a cron line.
# 19 Aug: MLS added so Spanish can be tested against a soccer crowd, which
# is where it will actually matter. CURATED with host/pick-slate.sh, not
# left wide open — eleven MLS matches against MAX_ROOMS=2 would put nine
# mute rooms on the rail, which is the RUN_LEAGUES bug reappearing one
# level down. host/slate-offer.js keeps the rail equal to the manifest.
# 20 Aug: MLB added. Thursday is the first live BASEBALL room this product
# has ever opened — Nationals @ Rangers 5:05pm PT, then 49ers @ Chargers at
# 7:00pm, two hours apart so one person can settle into the ballgame and then
# switch to the football room mid-evening. That cross-sport switch against two
# real rooms is the point of the night.
#
# THIS LINE ALONE IS NOT ENOUGH AND MUST NOT BE READ AS ENOUGH. Baseball plays
# fifteen games a day and most of them start in the morning, so with the global
# MAX_ROOMS the early games take every slot hours before the two games above are
# due. The pick file is what makes the night the night:
#     ~/gamenight-logs/slate-pick-2026-08-20.txt
# It names the two rooms, it wins over this variable in both build-slate.js and
# start-slate.sh, and it survives the 08:10 rebuild. Turning a league on here
# WITHOUT one is how a day gets eleven rooms nobody is hosting.
# 28 Aug: epl added here TOO, and it has to be — build-slate.js line 760
# filters the player's rail on RUN_LEAGUES, so a league that is built but
# not named here is invisible even when a pick file asks for it by id.
#
# THE ONE THING TO WATCH. English kick-offs land at 4:30, 6:00 and 7:00am
# Pacific, and the launcher now runs from 03:00. On a day WITH a pick file
# that is harmless — the pick file wins over this variable and nothing
# else starts. On a future EPL day with NO pick file, the morning fixtures
# become the day's rooms by default, hours before anyone is awake to play
# them.
#
# Monday 31 Aug is safe, but NOT because a pick file already exists — it
# does not. host/pick-monday-31aug.sh writes it at 08:20. What makes the
# window harmless is that nothing on Monday tips inside it: the EPL match
# is 12:00 PT and the earliest of twelve MLB games is 15:05 PT, and the
# launcher only starts a room near its tip. Do not read that as a general
# guarantee — it is true of this Monday's fixture list, not of the design.
# The weekend-morning question — when this system should wake up — is
# still an open decision and deserves its own night.
RUN_LEAGUES="wnba nfl mlb mls epl cfb"

# ======================================================================
# HOW A NIGHT'S ROOMS ARE CHOSEN — the rule, from the founder, 20 Aug 2026
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is not enforced in code; it is how the pick file gets written, and
# it belongs next to the cap because the two decide the night together.
#
# 1. THE WNBA IS THE MAIN SPORT AND GOES FIRST.
#    "Besides that everyday they have a national game we should have the
#    WNBA." Every day they play a NATIONAL game, they get a room — and we
#    take ALL of the national ones, not just one.
#
# 2. NATIONAL MEANS NATIONAL. USA Network, ESPN, CBS, ABC, NBC, NBA TV,
#    ION, Peacock/NBCSN, CNBC. It does NOT mean CW26 (Chicago), Fox 12 Plus
#    (Portland), NBC Sports Boston, KPIX+, Victory+, or League Pass — those
#    are regional affiliates and a room nobody outside that market can watch
#    is a room nobody plays.
#
# 3. PRIME VIDEO IS EXCLUDED, for now. "all national WNBA games except for
#    Prime for right now."
#
# 4. IF THERE IS NO QUALIFYING WNBA GAME, THE SLOT GOES TO ANOTHER SPORT.
#    "Yes if there is no WNBA we do another game." The night keeps its room
#    count; it does not shrink because one league is unavailable.
#    Worked example — Sat 22 Aug: both national WNBA games were on Prime, so
#    the WNBA room came out and Bills at Browns (10:00, NFL Network) went in.
#    It opens the day three hours before the next room rather than colliding
#    with one, which is the tie-breaker when choosing a substitute.
#
# 5. STAGGER, ALWAYS. Rooms an hour or more apart so a person can actually
#    move between them. Two rooms at the same time is one room and a
#    distraction. When a sport has a pile-up — eight NFL kickoffs at 10:00 PT
#    on a Sunday — the pick file names ONE of them.
#
# 6. DIFFERENT SPORTS WHERE POSSIBLE, THE SAME SPORT WHERE NOT.
#    A second room earns its cost when it is a different game to move to.
#    But on a day when one league is all that plays — baseball in early
#    September, soccer on an MLS Saturday — two rooms of that sport is
#    correct and better than one. "the days the mls is on when there is no
#    other games we do multiple MLS games and MLB games its fine."
# ======================================================================

# Most rooms live AT ONCE, across all leagues — not per league, not per day.
# The ceiling is Firestore reads, and it is lower than it looks:
#   runner alone            ~2,880 reads/room-night  ->  ~15 rooms/day
#   runner + watch-night.js ~5,610 reads/room-night  ->  ~8  rooms/day
# against a 50,000/day free tier that resets at midnight Pacific. When it
# runs out, claimLease throws, every runner dies at once, and every phone
# in every room stops together — including the flagship, killed by rooms
# nobody was sitting in. Raise this deliberately, with the watchdog in mind.
# 19 Aug: 2 -> 3. Three SLATE rooms tonight (Tempo@Mystics 4:30, LAFC@COL
# 6:30, SJ@LA 7:30) plus the flagship, which runs from its own cron line
# and does not spend a slot. At 2 the launcher would have started the two
# EARLIEST and silently refused SJ @ LA — the FS1 match — with nothing but
# a log line. Four concurrent rooms is ~27,400 Firestore reads, 55% of the
# free tier, against a measured ceiling of ~8 rooms with the watchdog on.
# This is also the first night four rooms have ever run at once: read
# SB.budget() from a phone console at full time and replace this estimate
# with a real number before 29 Aug.
# STRESS TEST WEEK, 20-24 Aug 2026. Founder: "This remainder of the week is
# our stress test, then next week we can go back to one or two, but now we
# stress test as much as we can. Remember all the users right now are beta
# testers."
#
# Raised 3 -> 4 for one reason: Saturday 22 Aug is the first day all four
# leagues play, and the marquee has already picked one room per sport. At 3
# the launcher would silently drop one of them, and which one it dropped
# would be whichever tipped last — the MLS match, which is the sport with
# the least evidence behind it and the one the Spanish work is aimed at.
#
# FROM MONDAY 24 AUG: 3, NOT 2. Founder, 20 Aug: "we dont have to do 2 games,
# we can do three starting next week that has each sport until soccer."
#
# Three rooms, ONE PER SPORT — which is the pairing rule at full width rather
# than a raised cap. NFL, MLB and WNBA are the three that play every day right
# now; MLS is away until 29 Aug, and when it returns this decision gets made
# again rather than quietly becoming four.
#
# Three is also what the read budget was built around, and it is what Friday
# 21 Aug already does: Jets at Steelers 4:00, Angels at Rangers 5:15, Fire at
# Tempo 7:00 — staggered ~75 minutes apart so one person can follow all three.
#
# REVERSED AGAIN, same day, an hour later. Founder: "We shouldn't have a
# limit on rooms. Right now were at 4 but in the future it may be more. so
# dont make any issues for the future."
#
# Every number this file has ever held for MAX_ROOMS — 2, 3, 4 — was a
# GUESS about how many rooms the real constraint could hold, picked by a
# person and then hand-raised again each time the business grew. That is
# exactly the shape of bug this project keeps finding: a policy standing
# in for a measurement. The actual constraint that ended a night — 19 Aug,
# GN13 — was never room count. It was CONCURRENT SNAPSHOT LISTENERS
# crossing ~78, and that number does not care whether it came from 2 rooms
# with a leak or 8 rooms without one.
#
# So MAX_ROOMS stops being the thing that decides this. host/start-slate.sh
# now asks host/listeners.js for the REAL, LIVE listener count before
# starting each room and refuses only if that number is already at/above
# 55 (the same alert threshold host/read-alert.js pages on) — the actual
# wall, measured, not a room-count guess about the wall. Growth from here
# is automatic: more rooms are fine for as long as real usage says they're
# fine, and nobody has to remember to edit this file again to allow a 5th.
#
# MAX_ROOMS=0 means exactly what it always meant two lines below in
# start-slate.sh — "0 = no cap" — and now that's the real setting, not a
# default nobody chose. It stays readable and settable here only as a
# manual override: set it back to a number by hand for one night if you
# specifically want a hard room-count ceiling regardless of listener
# headroom (e.g. testing, or distrust of a not-yet-proven measurement).
#
# Thursday 27 Aug's four picked rooms are still the first real test of
# this at scale either way — see host/listeners.js and the standing watch
# via host/listener-watch.js. If the listener gate is wrong about the real
# ceiling, that night is exactly where it will show, and the read-alert
# email fires independently of anything in this file.
MAX_ROOMS=0

# ── RULE 7: EVERY ROOM IS A NATIONALLY CARRIED GAME ──────────────────────
# Founder, 20 Aug 2026: "then we dont use that game. Make sure they are
# national games. our schedule should reflect that and be around that."
#
# Saturday 22 Aug was picked with Saints at Rams in the 1:00 PT slot. Its only
# carriage was ESPN Unlimited plus KCBS in Los Angeles and Fox 8 in New
# Orleans. A reader in Chicago would have been handed a room for a game they
# had no way to watch, which fails the one thing the product is for. Giants at
# Dolphins is the same 4:00 ET kickoff on NFL Network. The swap cost nothing,
# which is the point: on a full slate there is almost always a national game
# in the same slot, and picking the wrong one is carelessness, not scarcity.
#
# THE BAR IS NATIONAL LINEAR:
#   NFL Network · FOX · FS1 · CBS · CBS Sports Net · NBC · ABC · ESPN · ESPN2
#   ION · TNT · TBS · MLB Network · NBA TV · The CW · Peacock · Netflix
#
# NOT NATIONAL, whatever else is listed beside them:
#   any local affiliate (KCBS-TV, Fox 8, WUSA9, CBS4, KPIX+, NBC Sports Boston)
#   any team-owned channel (Nationals.TV, Rangers Sports Network, BravesVision)
#   ESPN Unlimited on its own. It is a paid add-on, not a channel people have.
#
# THE ONE EXCEPTION is a league with no linear option at all. Every MLS game is
# Apple TV and Friday MLB is Apple TV exclusive, so refusing streamers there
# would refuse the sport. A streamer is acceptable ONLY when the league has no
# linear game that day. Prime stays excluded for the WNBA under rule 3.
#
# host/build-slate.js checks this on every build and names any picked room that
# fails. It warns rather than refuses, because a build that silently drops a
# room is worse than one that runs and complains, but a warning here means the
# pick is wrong and should be changed before the email goes out.
